 "description": "Proctor2012 - Role of Amyloid-beta dimers in aggregation formation\nBioModels BIOMD0000000462 (curated). SBML file: BIOMD0000000462_url.xml.\nSimulation: 0 to 100000 time units (SED-ML: BIOMD0000000462_url.sedml (auto-generated placeholder); duration chosen from the dynamics: still changing at cap), sampling 100.\nRun switches: -ig:mass -INT:5 -obeymaxint\nVerification against libRoadRunner (SBML reference): PASS, max |difference| = 6.44e-07 of species peak (worst: Abeta)\nSBML time units are used unchanged as Kintecus seconds.\nConversion notes:\n  [info] 'AbDim' goes below zero in the SBML: integrated as AbDim_o = value + 0.002, output as AbDim = OUTC[AbDim_o;-0.002*source]\n  [info] AbetaDimerisation: rate order differs from the stoichiometry; consumed on separate line(s) - Abeta: first order\n  [info] AbetaPlaqueGrowth: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\nRenamed species (Kintecus name = SBML id): Source1 = Source; Sink1 = Sink",
